WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.933
The Document Object Model represents a page as a tree of objects.

00:00:03.933 --> 00:00:06.555
An event reports an interaction or other occurrence.

00:00:06.555 --> 00:00:10.160
Event handlers can update state and change what the browser displays.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.420
A displayed change does not automatically mean data was saved on the server.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.167
Activation is the input event.

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:21.010
A state value such as answerVisible changes from false to true.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.456
The explanation appearing on screen is output.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:29.395
If the page refreshes and no persistence was used, the state may return to its initial value.

00:00:30.395 --> 00:00:32.339
What does an event handler do?

00:00:32.339 --> 00:00:37.200
A handler responds to an event; its actual effects depend on the code it runs.
